function.arguments:
{
  "formation_name": "Overlapping PD Wall",
  "rationale": "Sovereign (toughest hull) pushed to +x as the vanguard to eat the first exchange. Falchions screen ahead-left/ahead-right of her, ~55-65 km off-axis so their point-defense envelopes overlap the battleship and each other. The three Lancers form a second gunline 50 km back and spread laterally (±70 km), still inside the ~100 km PD net, giving me a wide overlapping defensive umbrella while presenting three separated spinal threats. Modest z-staggering breaks a flat plane without opening PD gaps.",
  "placements": [
    { "ship_name": "OCS Sovereign", "x_km": 20, "y_km": 0, "z_km": 0 },
    { "ship_name": "OCS Falchion-1", "x_km": 5, "y_km": -60, "z_km": 10 },
    { "ship_name": "OCS Falchion-2", "x_km": 5, "y_km": 60, "z_km": -10 },
    { "ship_name": "OCS Lancer-1", "x_km": -30, "y_km": -70, "z_km": 20 },
    { "ship_name": "OCS Lancer-2", "x_km": -35, "y_km": 0, "z_km": 0 },
    { "ship_name": "OCS Lancer-3", "x_km": -30, "y_km": 70, "z_km": -20 }
  ]
}

{"ship_name": "OCS Sovereign", "order_text": "PHASE 1 — ADVANCE. Maneuver: INTERCEPT on the threat axis, 100% throttle (1.0g). Drive toward the enemy wall to close 441 -> ~150 km. Keep the bow locked on the nearest corvette (Dart-1) so we present minimal cross-section; hold a tight wall formation with the Lancers and Falchions, overlapping PD coverage toward the enemy.

WEAPONS: Spinal Coiler Mk3 — continuous fire on TIS Dart-1 (nearest corvette), re-engaging Dart-2 the instant Dart-1 is destroyed or breaks. Hold the heavy and light coilgun batteries for terminal PD unless a clean shot at a closing corvette opens inside 200 km.

Do NOT PADLOCK yet — we must close distance. At ~150 km I will signal PADLOCK and hold the wall. If any enemy torpedo launch is detected, go EVASIVE and let the wall's PD concentrate on the torpedo corridor. Abort/withdraw on fleet signal if we lose 2 ships before clearing half the enemy.", "priority": "CRITICAL", "suggested_target": "TIS Dart-1"}

{"ship_name": "OCS Lancer-2", "order_text": "Phase 1 continues. INTERCEPT TIS Dart-1 as part of Team A (with Sovereign and Lancer-1). Set heading directly at Dart-1 (bearing ~267,1,0 toward -168,31,10) and hold nose-on to the enemy axis to minimize cross-section. Throttle 67% - matched to the wall, do NOT outrun Sovereign or Lancer-1. Maintain tight wall formation, no independent maneuvering.

Weapons: hold spinal Coiler and both Coilgun Batteries on FIRE_WHEN_OPTIMAL, focused on Dart-1. Do not fire early - wait for the optimal solution; primary spinal shot is reserved for Dart-1.

WARNING: watch each checkpoint for enemy torpedo launches. If a salvo appears, immediately execute EVASIVE while the wall's PD concentrates on the torpedo corridor - do not fly straight into a salvo. Otherwise continue closing.", "priority": "HIGH", "suggested_target": "TIS Dart-1"}

{"ship_name": "OCS Falchion-2", "order_text": "INTERCEPT, nose-on, 50% throttle (matched wall speed) - stay in the wall line, do NOT open the formation. Target: TIS Dart-2 (Team B fires with Lancer-3 and Falchion-1). Hold fire until optimal range (inside ~150 km, Phase 2 PADLOCK), then commit spinal + Coilgun Battery Mk3 on Dart-2.

IMPORTANT: OCS Falchion-1 is under torpedo attack and evading - she will be maneuvering inside the wall. Give her lateral room, keep your station, and do NOT mirror her evasive moves; you stay on the wall line. All 13 PD turrets are massed on the inbound torpedo corridor - if any torpedo salvo is detected at this checkpoint, shift your PD to the corridor immediately and keep closing.

Watch for a second torpedo salvo every checkpoint; if YOU are targeted, evade hard while staying inside the wall's PD envelope. Do not slow the advance. FIRE_WHEN_OPTIMAL.", "priority": "HIGH", "suggested_target": "TIS Dart-2"}

{"ship_name": "OCS Falchion-2", "order_text": "HOLD THE WALL — do not string out. INTERCEPT TIS Dart-2 at 50% throttle, matching the fleet wall's closure rate; stay mutually inside point-defense range of Lancer-3 and the rest of the formation on the enemy threat axis. Keep nose-on to Dart-2 for the spinal Coiler Mk3. Do NOT chase receding hulls.

Weapons: hold fire until inside ~120 km, then FIRE_IMMEDIATE with the Spinal Coiler Mk3 as the primary, Coilgun Battery Mk3 as follow-up. You and Lancer-3 are the Dart-2 kill pair — coordinate your shot timing with Lancer-3 so your rounds land together and split their point defense.

If Dart-2 dies, shift immediately to the next nearest CLOSING corvette (nearest-first, nose-on) without breaking the wall. If you are newly targeted by a torpedo salvo, go EVASIVE inside the wall and let the fleet PD concentrate on that corridor — but return to INTERCEPT and the wall the moment the salvo is defeated. Report when Dart-2 is inside 120 km.", "priority": "HIGH", "suggested_target": "TIS Dart-2"}

{"ship_name": "OCS Lancer-1", "order_text": "EVASIVE — you are under torpedo attack. Execute jinking, unpredictable evasive burns at ~70% throttle to throw off seeker lead; the fleet PD wall is blinding the inbound torpedo corridor, so your job is to dodge the coasting wrecks, NOT to run. Do NOT break away from the wall or chase receding hulls.

While evading, keep nose-on alignment toward TIS Dart-1 (currently 76 km, closing) — this is your PRIMARY. Bring the Spinal Coiler Mk3 and both Coilgun Battery Mk3s to bear and FIRE_IMMEDIATE the instant you have alignment. Any fire window during your evasive pattern goes to Dart-1 first; only if Dart-1 dies or goes cold do you shift to the next NEAREST CLOSING corvette (Dart-2 at 85 km), nearest-first. Never engage a receding hull.

Hold your evasive pattern until the torpedo wave is past, then report status and resume wall station on my next order. No spinal shots wasted on non-closing targets.", "priority": "CRITICAL", "suggested_target": "TIS Dart-1"}

{"ship_name": "OCS Falchion-2", "order_text": "EVASIVE, HOLD THE WALL — do NOT chase. You are the anchor of the PD cluster and three guided torpedoes are still inbound on you: continuous random-walk evasion at 100% effectiveness, no straight-line legs, keep your thrust vector changing every few seconds so the coasting wreck and any live seekers miss. Stay inside the wall: do not let your separation from the main body exceed 250 km — if you drift, thrust to regain station, but keep total closure on the swarm at ZERO. Do not INTERCEPT any Dart; they are separating at 0.3-1.9 km/s and our hulls cannot run down 3.0g corvettes — pursuit only bleeds delta-v and opens the PD gap.

FIRE: spinal Coiler Mk3 + Coilgun Battery Mk3, FIRE_WHEN_OPTIMAL, nose and tubes oriented toward the swarm. Primary target Dart-8 (293 km, nearest presenting hull) — take the shot the instant you have a solution. If Dart-8 goes dark or leaves the envelope, shift to Dart-7. Do not sacrifice wall geometry for a shot; a held position with clean PD coverage is worth more than one marginal hit.

TORPEDOES: none — do not launch, we have no rounds. Your job is to stay alive, stay in the cluster, and keep your spinal guns speaking. Report any torpedo detonation or new inbound track immediately.", "priority": "CRITICAL", "suggested_target": "TIS Dart-8", "torpedo_salvo": 0}
